spec:
  id: knowledge_atoms
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Ontology
  compiler_stage: Knowledge Representation
  description: >
purpose[2]: Represent engineering knowledge at its,minimum reusable semantic granularity.
philosophy[4]: Tokens build language.,Instructions build programs.,Atoms build molecules.,Knowledge Atoms build engineering intelligence.
definition[5]: A Knowledge Atom is the smallest,engineering concept that possesses,independent meaning and cannot be,decomposed further without losing,semantic integrity.
model[13]: Knowledge Atom,→,Concept,→,Mechanism,→,Principle,→,Engineering Knowledge Record,→,Engineering Episode,→,Engineering World
properties[8]: Atomic,Immutable Identity,Explainable,Reusable,Composable,Versioned,Graph Native,Language Independent
types:
  description: Lesson
  examples: Measure Before Optimizing
atom[13]: identity,definition,purpose,mechanism,assumptions,prerequisites,dependencies,constraints,tradeoffs,examples,failure_modes,relationships,validation
attributes[7]: domain,capability,reasoning,difficulty,confidence,maturity,abstraction
relationships[12]: depends_on,requires,extends,specializes,causes,prevents,enables,optimizes,validates,measures,contradicts,complements
composition[7]: Knowledge Atoms,→,Concepts,→,Engineering Principles,→,Engineering Knowledge Records
examples:
  KA_000001:
    name: Mutex
    type: Concept
    purpose: Mutual Exclusion
    enables: Thread Safety
  KA_000002:
    name: Deadlock
    type: Failure
    caused_by: Circular Wait
  KA_000003:
    name: Locality
    type: Principle
    optimizes: Cache Performance
  KA_000004:
    name: Hash Table
    type: Mechanism
    requires: Hash Function
quality[6]: Single Responsibility,Single Meaning,Explicit Definition,Explicit Relationships,Engineering Value,Reusable
validation[6]: Every atom has one identity.,Every atom has one definition.,Every atom belongs to one domain.,Every atom has explicit relationships.,Every atom is reusable.,Every atom is independently understandable.
graph[6]: No isolated atoms.,Every atom participates,in at least one relationship.,Every atom contributes,to one or more Engineering,Knowledge Records.
evolution[7]: Knowledge Atoms may,gain relationships,improve definitions,gain examples,improve validation,Knowledge Atoms may never,lose identity
engineering[6]: Reusable,Explainable,Searchable,Linkable,Composable,Machine Interpretable
success[4]: Every engineering concept,can be represented,using one or more,Knowledge Atoms.
guarantees[5]: Universal Engineering Vocabulary,Minimal Semantic Units,Graph Native Knowledge,Unlimited Composition,Cross Domain Reusability
future:
  graph_embeddings: true
  semantic_vectors: true
  automated_discovery: true
  lifelong_expansion: true
  ontology_growth: true
